    {
      "title": "Password Hashing with bcrypt and argon2",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 1,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Password Hashing with bcrypt and argon2",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Hash, never encrypt",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "One-way ==hash==: a stolen DB reveals no passwords",
                "Never store plaintext or fast hashes: MD5, SHA-256",
                "Salt is ==random per password==, stored inside the hash string",
                "Salt defeats rainbow tables; both libraries add it"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. bcrypt vs argon2",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "javascript",
              "lines": [
                "const h = await bcrypt.hash(pw, 12)",
                "await bcrypt.compare(pw, h)",
                "const a = await argon2.hash(pw)",
                "await argon2.verify(a, pw)"
              ],
              "note": "bcrypt: cost 12, each +1 doubles time, input cut at 72 bytes"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "",
                "bcrypt",
                "argon2id"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "Tuning",
                  "cost factor",
                  "memory, time, parallelism"
                ],
                [
                  "Hardware",
                  "CPU-only",
                  "memory-hard, resists GPUs"
                ],
                [
                  "Status",
                  "proven, ubiquitous",
                  "OWASP first choice"
                ],
                [
                  "Use for",
                  "existing apps",
                  "new projects"
                ]
              ],
              "highlightRow": 3
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Mistakes",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "diagram",
              "kind": "flow",
              "spec": {
                "nodes": [
                  {
                    "text": "Find user",
                    "ink": "blue"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "compare / verify",
                    "ink": "green"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "One generic error",
                    "sub": "bad email or password",
                    "ink": "red"
                  }
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Sync variants block the event loop",
                "Comparing hashes with `===` instead of compare/verify",
                "Cost too low",
                "Logging passwords",
                "Different errors for bad email vs bad password"
              ],
              "style": "cross",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Remember",
              "text": "Use ==argon2id== for new projects, async calls only, one generic login error."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Sessions vs JWT",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 2,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Sessions vs JWT",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Session vs JWT",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "{blue:Session}: server stores state (memory, Redis, DB)",
                "Cookie holds an ==opaque session ID==; logout deletes it",
                "{purple:JWT}: signed `header.payload.signature` with claims (`sub`, `exp`)",
                "Stateless: server only ==verifies the signature==",
                "Payload is encoded, ==not encrypted==: no secrets"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "",
                "Session",
                "JWT"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "Revocation",
                  "{green:Instant}",
                  "{red:Not before exp} without denylist"
                ],
                [
                  "Scaling",
                  "Needs shared store",
                  "No lookup"
                ]
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Cookies and Tokens",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "`httpOnly`: blocks JS access",
                "`secure`: HTTPS only",
                "`sameSite=lax` or `strict`: CSRF defense, plus `maxAge`",
                "localStorage tokens are readable by ==XSS==",
                "Short-lived access token + ==rotating refresh token=="
              ],
              "style": "check"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "javascript",
              "lines": [
                "const t = jwt.sign({ sub: id }, secret,",
                "  { expiresIn: '15m', algorithm: 'HS256' });",
                "jwt.verify(t, secret, { algorithms: ['HS256'] });"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Mistakes",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Long-lived JWTs",
                "Unpinned algorithms (`alg: none`, confusion attacks)",
                "JWT stored in localStorage",
                "`decode()` instead of `verify()`",
                "Session fixation: regenerate session ID on login"
              ],
              "style": "cross"
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Interview Point",
              "text": "**Revoke a JWT?** Short expiry plus denylist. **decode vs verify?** decode skips the signature check. **Why sameSite?** It blocks CSRF."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "helmet, Rate Limiting and Zod Validation",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 3,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "helmet, Rate Limiting and Zod Validation",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. helmet and CSP",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "`app.use(helmet())` sets security headers in ==one line==",
                "Adds CSP, HSTS, `X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff`, X-Frame-Options",
                "Removes the ==X-Powered-By== header",
                "==CSP== limits where scripts, styles and images load from: the main XSS mitigation"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "javascript",
              "lines": [
                "app.use(helmet.contentSecurityPolicy({",
                " directives: { defaultSrc: [\"'self'\"] }",
                "}));"
              ],
              "note": "tune CSP directives"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Rate Limiting",
              "ink": "orange"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "`app.use(rateLimit({ windowMs: 15*60*1000, limit: 100 }))` returns ==429== when exceeded",
                "Apply a {red:stricter limit} to `/login` and `/signup`",
                "Behind a proxy: `app.set('trust proxy', 1)`, or every client looks like **one IP**",
                "Multiple instances: use a ==Redis store=="
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "orange"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Zod Validation",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "`safeParse` returns a result and does not throw",
                "On failure return ==400== with `result.error`",
                "Unknown keys are **stripped**; `.strict()` rejects them",
                "`z.infer<typeof Schema>` derives the TypeScript type",
                "Validate ==params== and ==query== too, not only the body"
              ],
              "style": "check",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "javascript",
              "lines": [
                "const Schema = z.object({",
                " email: z.string().email(),",
                " age: z.number().int().min(18) });",
                "const result = Schema.safeParse(req.body);",
                "if (!result.success)",
                " return res.status(400).json(result.error);"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Server side only counts",
              "text": "Client validation is only ==UX==. Always validate on the **server**."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
